<title>JAPAN: Baht float move in right direction--Thai minister.</title>
<headline>Baht float move in right direction--Thai minister.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai Finance Minister Thanong Bidaya told reporters on Friday that the managed float of the baht was a move in the right direction and that it would not be too long before the baht's exchange rate settled down.  </p>
<p>Asked if he thought the baht's fall to record low levels on Friday and the floating of the currency had been damaging to the Thai economy, he said: &quot;I think it is (a move) in the right direction.&quot;</p>
<p>He also told reporters it would take some time for the baht to reach an equilibrium level, but that it should not be too long.</p>
</text>
